From 743e3855e87fb3feb9becafd70bbe730a279d601 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Forb Hidden Gems <348521123+ForbHiddenGems@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:47:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 29/29] Digidex: every Digimon, seen or owned, with its
 digivolutions

A Digidex row in the top menu (the box grows a row; the grid is 2 x 4 with
the new row's right cell skipped) opens a new screen (task 0x17): every
Digimon in id order on the left, the selected one's model turning on the
right, and its level, type, technique, what it digivolves from and, by DP,
into. Unmet Digimon are a black silhouette named "?????"; seen ones show
their name and model; owned ones their technique too.

What the tamer has met lives in the save itself, in GameState bytes the
game never touches (0xFD4..0x1003, 0x1048..0x1057; zero in every retail
save): a seen and an owned bit per Digimon id. Enemies are seen at battle
start; the roster counts as owned when the menu opens and at battle start;
a battle digivolution owns its new form. Every save starts empty.

Windows are the top menu's own box sprite drawn in slices to any size. The
model is fitted to its window from where its bones project. F2 (dev build)
gets a "Digidex: show all" box that shows every Digimon without changing
the save.

